It returns `echo.NewHTTPError(http.StatusInternalServerError, i.(error).Error())` — i.e. a 500 HTTP error whose message is the `error` value that the pool's `New` function produced (the pool's `New` returns an `error` when `gzip.NewWriterLevel`/`gzip.NewReader` fails). The code is:

    i := pool.Get()
    gr, ok := i.(*gzip.Reader)
    if !ok {
        return echo.NewHTTPError(http.StatusInternalServerError, i.(error).Error())
    }

Note it asserts `i.(error)` there, so a pool item that is neither `*gzip.Reader` nor `error` would panic — but for the default pool the only non-reader value is the error from `New`.

